    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Lean deliberately restricts F to recursively enumerable axiom sets proving the theorems of IΣ₁ and uses the provability predicate of the Craig presentation of F. That presentation preserves F’s theorems but fixes a particular formula for the reflection instances. Theorem 3 allows an arbitrary F(x); its base-theory requirement is on S, not on F."
    }
